<figure class="cache-figure" data-latency-diagnosis>
 <p class="figure-title">The same 100 ms can hide different delays</p>
 <div class="cache-controls"><label>Illustrative cause <select data-case><option value="queue">Waiting behind another command</option><option value="execute">Expensive command execution</option><option value="network">Delay outside command execution</option></select></label></div>
 <p class="figure-note">One request, left to right · fixed 0–100 ms scale</p>
 <div class="ops-latency-track" data-track aria-hidden="true"></div>
 <ol class="ops-latency-stages" data-stages></ol>
 <div class="ops-execution-window"><span>SLOWLOG measures this command’s execution</span><div class="ops-latency-track" data-execution aria-hidden="true"></div><strong data-time></strong></div>
 <p class="explanation" data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <figcaption>These are invented, fully known schedules, not timings inferred from a slow log. Each bar uses the same scale. The execution window excludes this request’s preceding queue wait and client/network work. Real systems need evidence to locate the delay; a short command execution alone does not identify the cause.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
import{latencyCases,latencyStages}from'../../lib/caching/operations.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-latency-diagnosis]').forEach(root=>{const select=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-case]')!;const render=()=>{const s=latencyCases[select.value];root.querySelector('[data-track]')!.innerHTML=s.times.map((t,i)=>`<i class="ops-phase-${i}" style="width:${t}%"></i>`).join('');root.querySelector('[data-stages]')!.innerHTML=s.times.map((t,i)=>`<li><i class="ops-phase-${i}"></i>${latencyStages[i]} <b>${t} ms</b></li>`).join('');root.querySelector('[data-execution]')!.innerHTML=`<i class="ops-phase-3" style="margin-left:${s.times.slice(0,3).reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)}%;width:${s.times[3]}%"></i>`;root.querySelector('[data-time]')!.textContent=`${s.times[3]} ms execution · 100 ms elapsed`;root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=s.evidence;};select.onchange=render;render();});
</script>
